# a directory
blog/static/img: directory in static/
  fix: keep the static files in static/ itself

# names embed leaves out or a URL escapes
blog/static/.keep: static file name ".keep" does not start with a letter or digit and hold only letters, digits, '.', '-' and '_'
  fix: rename it, such as app.css
blog/static/_draft.css: static file name "_draft.css" does not start with a letter or digit and hold only letters, digits, '.', '-' and '_'
  fix: rename it, such as app.css
blog/static/a b.css: static file name "a b.css" does not start with a letter or digit and hold only letters, digits, '.', '-' and '_'
  fix: rename it, such as app.css
blog/static/a:b.css: static file name "a:b.css" does not start with a letter or digit and hold only letters, digits, '.', '-' and '_'
  fix: rename it, such as app.css

# no file
blog/static: static/ holds no file to serve
  fix: add a file, or remove the directory: //go:embed needs one
blog/static/x: directory in static/
  fix: keep the static files in static/ itself

# a package without routes
lib/static: static/ of a package without routes
  fix: keep static files in an app with a route table, which serves them at /static/APP/ (D-137)
static: static/ of a package without routes
  fix: keep static files in an app with a route table, which serves them at /static/APP/ (D-137)

# two packages of one name
more/blog/static: apps blog and more/blog are both package blog, so both would serve /static/blog/
  fix: rename one package, or keep the static files in one of them

# routes under /static/
blog/urls.go:16:12: route path "/static/x" is under /static/, where maago serves the apps' static files (D-137)
  fix: move the route to another path
blog/urls.go:17:12: route path "/static" is under /static/, where maago serves the apps' static files (D-137)
  fix: move the route to another path

# a route the static files' pattern conflicts with
blog/urls.go:16:12: route GET /{x}/blog/a.css conflicts with /static/blog/{name}, where maago serves static files: a request could match both
  fix: make the route more specific than the static files' pattern, or move it

# a name the static files' code declares
blog/urls.go:11:5: the static files of app blog would declare maagoStatic, which blog/more.go:3 declares already
  fix: rename what else declares maagoStatic

# no static/, no pattern

